      <title>Failure to Hold Minimum Four Board Meetings as per S 173(1): MCA Imposes Penalty on Company and its Directors [Read Order]</title>
      <link>https://www.taxscan.in/top-stories/failure-to-hold-minimum-four-board-meetings-as-per-s-1731-mca-imposes-penalty-on-company-and-its-directors-1441766</link>
      <description>As per the provisions of Section 173(1) of the Companies Act, 2013, every company is required to hold a minimum of four meetings of its Board of Directors every year in such a manner that not more than 120 days shall intervene between two consecutive meetings of the Board.</description>
